Suggests: vinyl-cache-dev
Description: high-performance web accelerator (matrix build)
 Vinyl Cache is a high-performance HTTP accelerator. It stores responses in
 memory so origin servers do not have to produce the same response repeatedly.
 .
 This package contains the vinyld daemon, the command line utilities, the
 shared library, the VMODs distributed with Vinyl Cache and a systemd service
 adapted from the official Varnish package integration.
 .
 gcc and the C library headers are runtime dependencies because vinyld
 compiles each VCL program with the system toolchain at run time.

Package: vinyl-cache-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 vinyl-cache (= ${binary:Version}),
 pkgconf,
 python3,
Description: development files for Vinyl Cache (matrix build)
 Headers, the vinylapi.pc pkg-config file, the vinyl.m4 autoconf macros and
 the vmodtool.py/vsctool.py generators needed to build a Vinyl Cache VMOD or
 an application against libvinylapi.
 .
 A VMOD is bound to the exact Vinyl Cache build it was compiled against, so
 this package depends on the exact matching vinyl-cache binary version.
